      "dependency_name": "Resource availability",
      "dependency_description": "Availability of fuels for power generation and trade are bounded by proven reserves and existing renewable potential, with no assumed new exploration. Fossil fuel reliance means that ASEAN becomes a net importer of natural gas in 2027, while exporting coal until 2050. No hard limitation for scaling up power generation in BAS though.",
      "sector": "Power",
      "evidence_type": "Quantitative"
    },
    {
      "dependency_name": "Labor availability",
      "dependency_description": "BAS produces the smallest fossil-sector job losses, so workforce disruption is limited relative to the other pathways. But it also creates the least amount of new jobs in renewable energy.",
      "sector": "Power",
      "evidence_type": "Quantitative"
    }
  ],
